Package: ChiSquaredTools
Type: Package
Title: Chi-Squared Analysis Tools
Version: 1.2.0
Date: 2026-10-10
Author: Gianmarco Alberti
Maintainer: Gianmarco Alberti <gianmarcoalberti@gmail.com>
Description: Comprehensive toolkit for chi-squared analysis of contingency tables.
    Includes nine analytical facilities: (1) Chi-squared testing with traditional,
    (N-1)/N adjusted, permutation, Monte Carlo, and M test (maximum adjusted residual)
    methods; (2) Post-hoc analysis with cell-level metrics including standardised
    residuals, moment-corrected standardised residuals, adjusted standardised residuals,
    Quetelet Index, IJ association factor, backwards-stepping outlier detection, PEM
    with bootstrap confidence intervals, median polish residuals (standardised and
    adjusted), Goodman-Kruskal residuals, and Difference in Estimated Proportions (DEP);
    (3) Association measures with over 20 coefficients organised by statistical
    foundation, including chi-squared-based, margin-free, and PRE measures;
    (4) Power analysis for a priori sample size determination, post-hoc power
    calculation, and sensitivity analysis; (5) Simultaneous Reduction of Dimension (SRD) 
    for sparse contingency tables using hypothesis testing to merge statistically 
    indistinguishable rows and columns; (6) Hierarchical clustering using Ward's
    method with chi-squared distance, using significance testing or the inertia gain ratio; (7) Correspondence 
    Analysis with symmetric CA plot, geometric interpretation plot, and contribution 
    biplot, supporting both Pearson and Freeman-Tukey residuals with optional adjusted 
    standardised residuals; (8) Stratified analysis for 2x2xK tables with 
    Cochran-Mantel-Haenszel test, Breslow-Day-Tarone and Woolf homogeneity tests, and forest 
    plots; (9) Stratified analysis for RxCxK tables with generalised CMH test, 
    log-linear homogeneity test, and trajectory plots. Features toggleable method 
    explanations with rationale and usage guidance, automatic significance 
    highlighting, diagnostic decision trees, and proper academic citations.
